# OpenChange-UK compute

- The agent may run `clifton auth` to start the device-code/SSO flow; the human completes SSO approval interactively. After the resulting certificate is valid, ssh and Slurm commands (sbatch, srun, salloc, scancel, squeue, sacct, sinfo, scontrol) may be executed within these limits. Never run destructive filesystem commands.
- Never change a Slurm time limit above 30 minutes unless the human explicitly asks.
- Every training submission requires an explicit config file and a git commit hash.
- Every job log must include config path, git SHA, seed, environment, and, once training exists, metrics and checkpoint path.
- Never download a dataset inside a training job.
- Use dry-run mode and a hand-checked pilot of at most 500 samples before full training.
- Held-out geographic regions and future dates are immutable once the specification is accepted.
- Isambard-AI is aarch64 GH200. Use the documented NGC PyTorch image with Apptainer `--nv`. Do not pip-install an x86 torch wheel.
- If a partition or QOS name is not in the Isambard docs, say "verify in docs" instead of inventing one.
- Official source of truth: https://docs.isambard.ac.uk